/-!
# The six two-zero same-generator planes

The rows are (s+d*t,s-d*t,e*t,f*t), where (d,e,f) is a permutation of (1,2,3).
For d=1 use (s,t)=(3/7,1/7); for d=2 use (3/7,3/7); for d=3 use (3/7,2/7).
Every displayed coordinate has circle distance at least 2/7 at that one pair.
This covers exactly these six normalized planes; normalization and the
reduction from arbitrary planes are separate obligations.
-/

noncomputable section
namespace Math15.LonelyRunner

theorem torus_two_zero_123 :
    TorusGood (![1, 1, 0, 0]) (![1, -1, 2, 3]) (2 / 7) := by
  refine ⟨3 / 7, 1 / 7, ?_⟩
  intro i
